From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:39:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] update pause requeue: a Stop latched during the
 write cancels the head instead of running it after the hold

t_01a1d4a0ecd9bd54. ea4f9dc74e5 (t_01a1d49d50e4c656) makes a started notifier wake that gets the session lease
under a pending core-update pause yield before its turn and go back to its FIFO place (requeue_unstarted). That
closed the core ask of this card (laptop-1 2026-11-13 03:07:12 PST, chat 20261026_235722_bef6c6). One custody gap
from review 5890417193 of PR #2173 was still open on main:

A Stop (interrupt_update) that latches while the requeue write runs finds the claim still started and tells its
caller the turn stops. Main then discarded the latch with the claim, so the row stayed queued and the notice ran
after the hold. requeue_unstarted now reads stopped() before it clears the claim. If a Stop latched,
_stopped_after_requeue cancels the re-queued row (cancel_session_input, _settle_cancelled, media released),
answers the waiter and clears update_stops/pending_stops. A cancel failure logs loudly and leaves the row queued
(it then runs once after the hold, as before).

The bound-steer gap from the same review landed separately on main in d495dccb3fe, so this commit keeps main's
steer handling unchanged.

Tests: tests/gateway/test_update_requeue_stop_race.py is RED on origin/main (row stays queued) and GREEN here;
29 update-pause/requeue/notifier-drain files: 231 passed.
